{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/normalizedLaplacianEigenpairs(smallest:tolerance:maxIterations:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"normalizedLaplacianEigenpairs","kind":"identifier"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"smallest"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"tolerance"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","text":"Double"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"maxIterations"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int"},{"kind":"text","text":"?) "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols13NoConvergenceV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"NoConvergence"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:19SpectralGraphTheory10EigenpairsV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Eigenpairs"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"title":"normalizedLaplacianEigenpairs(smallest:tolerance:maxIterations:)","symbolKind":"method","externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P08SpectralA6TheoryE29normalizedLaplacianEigenpairs8smallest9tolerance13maxIterationsAD0G0VyxGSi_SdSiSgtAA13NoConvergenceVYKF","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/SpectralGraphTheory\/Eigenpairs.swift#L564","fileName":"Eigenpairs.swift"},"extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","roleHeading":"Instance Method","modules":[{"name":"SpectralGraphTheory","relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"]}]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"normalizedLaplacianEigenpairs","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"smallest","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"tolerance","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Double","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" = 1e-8, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"maxIterations","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"? = nil) ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"NoConvergence","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/NoConvergence","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols13NoConvergenceV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Eigenpairs","identifier":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/Eigenpairs","preciseIdentifier":"s:19SpectralGraphTheory10EigenpairsV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}]}]},{"kind":"parameters","parameters":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The number of eigenpairs, in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0...vertexCount"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"smallest"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The residual a Ritz pair must reach, relative as described above."}]}],"name":"tolerance"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The matrix–vector products each Lanczos run may spend; nil for the limits","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"under Throws.","type":"text"}]}],"name":"maxIterations"}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Return Value","level":2,"anchor":"return-value","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The eigenpairs, in order from that end of the spectrum."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Component by component: each component’s null vector first (eigenvalue 0, components in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order of their least vertex), then the smallest positive eigenvalues of the components"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"merged. On a component of at least 64 vertices, thick-restart Lanczos (Wu–Simon) with full"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reorthogonalization and locking, the null vector projected out, from a fixed start vector:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"on σI − M (σ Gershgorin’s bound) while σ\/λ₂ is moderate, else on M⁺ by shift-invert, each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"product a conjugate-gradient solve with L grounded at the vertex of largest degree. A Ritz"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pair is accepted when its residual is at most "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tolerance"},{"type":"text","text":" · λ, relative to itself as for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"algebraicConnectivity"},{"type":"text","text":"; the vectors found are then rotated by Rayleigh–Ritz on M, and each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"value is its vector’s Rayleigh quotient, a sum over edges. The dense solver on a smaller"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"component, or when k is a third of it or more."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"O((n + m) · products + n · k²) time, O(n · k) "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Double"},{"type":"text","text":"s for the vectors and n · max(30, 2k +"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"10) for the basis."}]},{"type":"aside","name":"Precondition","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"","type":"text"},{"code":"smallest","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is in ","type":"text"},{"code":"0...vertexCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"tolerance > 0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"code":"maxIterations","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"when given, is at least 1.","type":"text"}]}],"style":"note"},{"type":"aside","name":"Throws","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"","type":"text"},{"code":"NoConvergence","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" when a Lanczos run by shift-invert spends ","type":"text"},{"code":"maxIterations","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" products","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(1,000 when nil), or a conjugate-gradient solve inside it 20,000 + 2n iterations, without","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"converging. A run on σI − M hands over to shift-invert rather than throwing, after 4,000 +","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"20√n products or ","type":"text"},{"code":"maxIterations","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", whichever is smaller. The dense solver throws as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"laplacianSpectrum","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" does.","type":"text"}]}],"style":"note"}]}],"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/spectralgraphtheory\/graphprotocols\/graph\/normalizedlaplacianeigenpairs(smallest:tolerance:maxiterations:)"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The k smallest eigenvalues of the normalized Laplacian N ("},{"code":"normalizedLaplacianMatrix()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), k"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"= "},{"code":"smallest","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", ascending, each with a unit eigenvector (see "},{"code":"Eigenpairs","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory","doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"sections":[],"references":{"doc://SpectralGraphTheory/documentation/SpectralGraphTheory/Eigenpairs":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/Eigenpairs","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/spectralgraphtheory\/eigenpairs","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Eigenpairs"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Eigenpairs"}],"title":"Eigenpairs","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Eigenpairs of a graph matrix at one end of its spectrum: the eigenvalues, from that end"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(ascending for the smallest, descending for the largest), and an orthonormal eigenvector for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each, with one entry per vertex."}]},"doc://SpectralGraphTheory/documentation/SpectralGraphTheory/GraphProtocols/Graph":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Graph"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"extension"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P","kind":"identifier","text":"Graph"}],"url":"\/documentation\/spectralgraphtheory\/graphprotocols\/graph","abstract":[],"role":"symbol","title":"Graph"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/NoConvergence":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/NoConvergence","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/noconvergence","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kin